> We use kebab-casing in other URLs.

The config object parameter should be updated here. 

@saurabhg772244 blocker.

Blocking:

Please add a 3rd parameter to the function, to which we pass config as a field. It should be an object containing config, so that we can add more optional parameters easily. 
We are planning to remove the use of getConfig to allow parallel rendering soon. So adding more calls should be avoided. 

```suggestion
export const filledCircle = (parent: SVG, node: Node, { config: { themeVariables } }: { config?: MermaidConfig } = {} ) => {
  const { labelStyles, nodeStyles } = styles2String(node);
  node.label = '';
  node.labelStyle = labelStyles;
  const shapeSvg = parent
    .insert('g')
    .attr('class', getNodeClasses(node))
    .attr('id', node.domId ?? node.id);
  const radius = 7;
  const { cssStyles } = node;

  // @ts-ignore - rough is not typed
  const rc = rough.svg(shapeSvg);
```

```ts
  if (vertex?.img) { ... }
  if (vertex?.icon) { ... }
  if (vertex.type === 'square') { ... }
```

I'm not talking about the internals. Consider the above, the first 2 have `?`, while the 3rd one does not. So, there is no actual runtime safety if `vertex` is `undefined`, as even if the first two passes, third one will throw error as we're trying to access `type` of `undefined`. 

So, either we should enforce properly that vertex is never undefined, and remove the `?`s.
Or, we could do `if(!vertex) return`, and then remove the `?`s, or add `?` to all the required usecases.

```suggestion
  ```typescript
  import { myNewShape } from './shapes/myNewShape';

  const shapes = {
    ...,
    'my-new-shape': myNewShape,
    // Shortened alias (if any).
    'm-nsh': myNewShape
  };
  ```
```
